<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n17228" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτροφ-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>ill-fed,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				X.
				<u>Mem.</u>
				3.3.4
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ώτερος εἶναι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ael.
					<u>NA</u>
					12.20
				</span></i>
			; <i>ill of atrophy, pining away,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.912e
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b>
			<i>non-viable,</i> of infants, <i><span class="en">
				Ptol.
				<u>Tetr.</u>
				127
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				Act.
			, <i>not nutritious,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				2.5.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				2.6.4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Diph.Siph.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Ath.
				2.54a
			</span></i> (
				Comp.
			); so prob. in <i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Mete.</u>
				384a25
			</span></i> (but possibly, <i>that will not curdle</i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρέφω</span> I)). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἄτροφος τυρός: ὁ πησσόμενος</span> (
				Lacon.
			), <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i></div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
